# ⚠️ DELIBERATE — the level-by-level improvement run's evidence layer is LOCAL-ONLY.
# `backlogs/NN-<level>.md` holds playtest captures, diagnosis and costed items; it is
# development material, not something for viewers of the public repo. `CLAUDE.md` and
# `GAME_MECHANICS_IDEAS.md` §1a still describe and index it on purpose — a session needs to
# know it exists. Do not "fix" this by un-ignoring it; the rule is the user's call (2026-08-19).
# (The `BACKLOG.md` line above is a different, older file and is unrelated.)
backlogs

# ── assets_src — unprocessed originals ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTHING here is loaded by the game: every `assets_src` mention inside `game/` is a comment
# pointing at assets_src/README.md, never a `load()` or a path constant. What IS committed is
# the subset that an automated step reads as INPUT, so a fresh clone can still re-run every
# pipeline:
#   textures/level_3_corridor/vesper_note_paper_raw.jpg    tools/make_vesper_note.py:48
#   textures/level_3_corridor/screamer_false_door_raw.jpg  tools/make_false_door_screamer.py:65
#   textures/level_backrooms/backrooms_note_paper_raw.jpg  tools/make_backrooms_note.py:61
#   textures/level_1_lab/lab_breaker_panel_raw.png         tools/flatten_alpha_checker.py; also
#                                                          needed to re-prove check_nook_dark.gd's
#                                                          checkerboard limits (manual, line 218)
#   textures/intro/door_from_intro_to_lab.png              cutout_alpha.py -> restencil_door.py
#   textures/level_3_corridor/door_from_corridor_to_...    manual crop (assets_src/README.md)
#   audio/level_2_house/chase.wav                          tools/make_loop.py
# Everything else is local-only. It is still irreplaceable — the pipelines are destructive and
# generations are stochastic — but no automated step needs it, so it does not belong in a repo
# other people clone.
# ⚠️ A pattern here does NOT apply to a file git already tracks — `git check-ignore` will even
# stay silent about one (pass --no-index to test the pattern alone). Untracking therefore takes
# an explicit `git rm --cached`, which is how ALL FIVE video originals became local-only:
# fall_scene.mp4 and intro_scene.mp4 were committed for a while and were removed on 2026-08-19
# at the user's call. ⚠️ That was a decision about repo CONTENTS, not size — `git rm --cached`
# reclaims nothing, because the blobs stay in history permanently (which is why .git is 854 MB).
# Only a history rewrite changes that number.
# Still tracked despite matching nothing a tool reads: textures/superseded/* — see the section
# of assets_src/README.md that explains why a retired asset is kept.
assets_src/reference/
assets_src/video/seeds/
assets_src/video/*.mp4
assets_src/audio/**/*.flac
assets_src/**/*_pre2026-*
assets_src/textures/**/*_raw.*
# ⚠️ THE 91 MB EXCEPTION (2026-09-03). `assets_src/models/hollow_crown/` holds the six Meshy
# source GLBs that `tools/merge_creature_glb.py` reads as INPUT, so by this file's own rule
# ("committed if an automated step reads it") they should be tracked. They are not, and the
# reason is arithmetic: they are 15.2 MB EACH and identical apart from one animation track, so
# committing them would put 91 MB of duplicated mesh into a repo whose .git is already 854 MB —
# permanently, since a blob stays in history. The 9.8 MB merged artefact in
# `game/assets/models/hollow_crown.glb` IS committed and is what the game loads.
# ⚠️ CONSEQUENCE, stated so it is not discovered: the creature model cannot be re-merged from a
# fresh clone. Same trade as the five cutscenes, and `assets_src/README.md` records the SHA-256s
# so a re-download can be checked against what shipped.
assets_src/models/

# `tools/remaster_scares.py` copies each sting here before it overwrites it. Local-only: a safety
# net for the person running the tool, not an input to it — the tool refuses to re-process a file
# it has already processed, and the shipped audio is what the game loads.
assets_src/audio/pre_remaster/

# ⚠️ THE SUPPLIED CREATURE ZIP, 71 MB, AT THE REPO ROOT. Ignored for the same reason as
# `assets_src/models/` — it IS those six GLBs. A .gitignore block that spends ten lines
# explaining why 91 MB must never enter history, while the same bytes sit unignored one
# directory up, is not a rule. (Found by an audit probe, 2026-09-03.)
Meshy_AI_*.zip
# `tools/remaster_scares.py` copies each sting here before it overwrites it. Local-only: they are
# a safety net for the person running the tool, not an input to it — the tool refuses to
# re-process a file it has already processed, and the shipped audio is what the game loads.
assets_src/audio/pre_remaster/hollow_crown/` holds the six Meshy
# source GLBs that `tools/merge_creature_glb.py` reads as INPUT, so by this file's own rule
# ("committed if an automated step reads it") they should be tracked. They are not, and the
# reason is arithmetic: they are 15.2 MB EACH and identical apart from one animation track, so
# committing them would put 91 MB of duplicated mesh into a repo whose .git is already 854 MB —
# permanently, since a blob stays in history. The 9.8 MB merged artefact in
# `game/assets/models/hollow_crown.glb` IS committed and is what the game loads.
# ⚠️ CONSEQUENCE, stated so it is not discovered: the creature model cannot be re-merged from a
# fresh clone. Same trade as the five cutscenes, and `assets_src/README.md` records the SHA-256s
# so a re-download can be checked against what shipped.
assets_src/models/
